<title>USA: Marathon Oil cuts U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts.</title>
<headline>Marathon Oil cuts U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX Corp, said it had lowered the price it will pay for most U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Monday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $18.50 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $16.65 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is cut 50 cents now $18.25 and Oklahoma sweet is $18.50.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
